**Fleet host (Hari):** the global/fleet dashboard is a separate, run-once deployment. On the host that owns the **fleet domain**, invoke **Hari** to stand up the central collector (`.cursor/central/`) with TLS, so all worker VPSs can push to one board at `https://<fleet-domain>/`. Hari is **not** part of the per-project pipeline and does not use the Context Agent. Worker runs only need to be given the fleet domain at kickoff; Maya fetches the push token from `/api/fleet-config` automatically (and retries if Hari has not deployed yet).

> **Never auto-launch Hari.** The `fleet-host-agent` file ships in the shared `.cursor/` on **every** VPS (workers included), but it is **inert** — it runs only on an explicit operator request to deploy the fleet board, on the host the operator designates. The per-project workflow below never includes Hari. When a worker run is asked only to "build the backend", do **not** invoke Hari; just have Maya push to the already-running fleet host.

